    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d184">

                <pb facs="0319" n="223" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg223"/>

                <head>No. 184.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Francis to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1871-11-08"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 8, 1871</date>.
                        (Received December 7.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 3.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit the text of
                    the recent speech of the King of Greece, at the opening of the session of the
                    chamber of deputies, on the 30th of October ultimo, of which my predecessor, Mr.
                    Tuckerman, gave a brief synopsis in his dispatch (No. 188) of the date of
                    November 3.</p>
                <p>Inclosed is a printed copy of the speech, in French, with accompanying
                    translation into English.</p>
                <p>His Majesty’s reference to brigandage is worthy of attention.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN M. FRANCIS.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d184-a1.xml" xpointer="d184-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
